{
  "_meta": {
    "issue": 928,
    "seeded": "2026-09-24 no-key local run (M-class arm64), --tags integration --exclude-tags browser-ext,llm",
    "reseated": "gh-1005 (2026-09-30): the gate's measurement environment moved with its leg mac -> hosted linux (pty-integration-linux, ubuntu-24.04-arm). Re-seeded from a full-manifest no-key run on a linux x64 runner-class host (--tags integration --exclude-tags browser-ext, --concurrency=4, json file-reporter): budget = measured x 1.5 — a hardware-class buffer until keyed arm64 runner data lands (x64-hosted vs Graviton skew is inside it). headless_tools_flag uses the clean-env green total; all other suites ran green in the base run.",
    "metric": "suite total = sum of per-test spans (dart test json reporter)",
    "seed_policy": "suites budgeted ONLY when every test passed locally with a meaningful span (sub-second totals are silent early-return skips, not measurements)",
    "provisional": "budgets tighten from RUNNER-class data: download the integration-json-shard-* artifacts from a keyed ci.yml pty-integration-linux run and run scripts/check_test_durations.py --update-baseline on them in a reviewed PR (ratchet only tightens); any suite needing a HIGHER budget than this seed requires a hand-edited reviewed PR",
    "ratchet": "down-only via check_test_durations.py --update-baseline; raises require a hand-edited reviewed PR",
    "note": "no scheduled workflow writes this file",
    "removed": "pr-1294 (2026-10-06): test/integration/dap_cli_e2e_test.dart budget (140.1 s) removed — the suite is flake-quarantined out of the gate legs (scripts/test_quarantine.json, gh-1293), so its absence tripped the budgeted-suite-did-not-run check. Returns unbudgeted (nightly-visible) until the gh-1293 fix lands; re-budget from the nightly integration-json artifact in the un-quarantine PR."
